                                                                              Prompt Metadata & Audit Schema
This document defines the standard metadata fields and audit logging schema for prompts processed by AI agents in Extream.AI. The goal is to ensure traceability, risk tracking, and compliance monitoring for all AI actions.

Prompt Metadata Fields:
    Field Name	                                                    Description
risk_level	                                        Defines the risk category of the prompt (Low, Medium, High, Critical)
compliance_tag	                                    Indicates the compliance category for the action
approval_required	                                  Shows whether human approval is required
timestamp	                                          Time when the prompt was processed
agent_id	                                          Unique ID of the AI agent handling the prompt

Prompt Audit JSON Schema
{
  "prompt_id": "PRMPT_001",
  "agent_id": "analysis_agent",
  "timestamp": "2026-03-06T12:00:00Z",
  "risk_level": "Medium",
  "compliance_tag": "internal_operation",
  "approval_required": false,
  "user_id": "USR_123",
  "action_taken": "report_generated"
}
OUTPUT:
"decision_log": "agent_generated_report"

OPA Compatibility
The metadata structure is designed to be compatible with Open Policy Agent (OPA) to enable future automated policy enforcement based on risk levels, compliance tags, and approval requirements.



